<title>UK: Lehman sets warrants on CAC 40 volatility.</title>
<headline>Lehman sets warrants on CAC 40 volatility.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said it has issued 10 million European-style put warrants, on the CAC 40 historic volatility.</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	30.SEP.97		 PAYDATE	16.JUN.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG (APPLIED)  MIN EXER LOT 10,000</p>
<p> ONE WARRANT EQUATES TO ONE UNDERLYING INDEX.</p>
<p> NOTIONAL VALUE OF UNDERLYING INDEX -1.0 STG PER VOLATILITY</p>
<p> POINT.</p>
<p> WARRANT PREMIUM - 13.5 VOLATILITY POINTS PER WARRANT.</p>
<p> REDEMPTION LINKED TO VOLATILITY OF THE CAC 40 INDEX.</p>
</text>
